---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
---
<Base title={"For Hotel Owners"} description={"Options for hotel owners facing a loan maturity or default."}>
<Hero eyebrow={"For hotel owners"} title={"A hotel loan in default does not have to end in foreclosure."} lead={"When a lender will not extend and a refinance will not cover the balance, there are still negotiated ways through. We provide the capital that makes them possible."}>
  <a class="btn btn-light arrow" href="/contact/">Discuss your loan</a>
</Hero>
<main id="main">
<section class="section"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Paths to resolution</p><h2>What can happen to a troubled hotel loan, and where we come in.</h2></div>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Path</th><th scope="col">What it means</th><th scope="col">Our role</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Discounted payoff</th><td>The lender agrees to accept less than the full balance in exchange for payment now.</td><td>We fund the payoff.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Note purchase</th><td>The lender sells the loan. The new holder steps into its position under the same documents.</td><td>We buy the loan and work with the owner on new terms.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Recapitalization</th><td>New capital enters to cure the default and fund the brand's improvement plan.</td><td>We invest alongside the owner.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Consensual transfer</th><td>The owner hands over the hotel by agreement, often in exchange for a release from the guaranty.</td><td>We structure the transfer after acquiring the loan.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section alt"><div class="wrap intro">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">If we acquire your loan</p><h2>What changes, and what does not.</h2>
    <div class="body"><p>When a loan is sold, the loan documents stay the same. Your obligations and rights are the ones already in the note, mortgage, and any guaranty.</p>
    <p>What changes is who makes the decisions. A buyer that acquired the loan at a different basis often has room to agree to terms the original lender could not.</p></div></div>
  <dl class="pillars">
    <div><dt>We make contact directly</dt><dd>You hear from a principal of the firm, with notice of the transfer and where payments go.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>We ask for current information</dt><dd>Operating statements, performance reports, and the status of the franchise.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>We propose a resolution</dt><dd>A modification, a payoff figure, or a negotiated transfer, put in writing.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>We prefer agreement</dt><dd>Negotiated outcomes are faster and cost both sides less. Where no agreement can be reached, we rely on the rights in the loan documents.</dd></div>
  </dl>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">What to have ready</p><h2>Information that lets us respond quickly.</h2></div>
  <div class="cells two">
    <div><h3>The loan</h3><ul><li>Current lender and outstanding balance</li><li>Maturity date and payment status</li><li>Any forbearance or modification in place</li><li>Whether the loan is guaranteed</li></ul></div>
    <div><h3>The hotel</h3><ul><li>Brand, location, and room count</li><li>Trailing twelve-month operating statement</li><li>Recent performance reports</li><li>The improvement plan and its deadline</li></ul></div>
  </div>
  <p class="fine">Nothing here is legal advice. Owners should consult their own counsel before negotiating with a lender.</p>
</div></section>
</main>
<Cta title={"Talk through your loan with a principal."} text={"Conversations are confidential and carry no obligation."} label={"Discuss your loan"} />
</Base>
